---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HotelRow from '../components/HotelRow.astro';
import { hotels } from '../data/hotels';

const title = 'Best Hotels in Goa: 10 Stays to Compare | Goa, Considered';
const description = 'Compare 10 curated Goa stays across North, South and Central Goa by location, listed facilities, trip fit and practical trade-offs.';
const itemList = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ItemList',
  name: 'Curated selection of ten Goa hotels — editorial reading order',
  itemListElement: hotels.map((hotel, index) => ({
    '@type': 'ListItem',
    position: index + 1,
    item: { '@type': 'Hotel', name: hotel.name },
  })),
};
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="google-site-verification" content="oTFy51HrtVRxUPB8kfpuJFMPWsEjZncO0Xk5oqWN_CY" />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemList)} />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="kicker">A considered guide to Goa stays</p>
      <h1>10 Best Hotels in Goa</h1>
      <p class="lead">Ten Goa stays, from beach resorts to city bases. Compare location, listed facilities, trip fit and practical trade-offs.</p>
      <div class="intro-note">A curated selection; numbers indicate reading order, not a proven quality rank.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="hotel-selection">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">The shortlist</p>
          <h2>Ten Goa stays</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Search and filter to narrow the list.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="toolbar" aria-label="Filter hotel list">
        <label class="sr-only" for="hotel-search">Search stays</label>
        <input id="hotel-search" data-search type="search" placeholder="Search hotel, area or feature" />
        <label class="sr-only" for="region-filter">Filter by region</label>
        <select id="region-filter" data-region>
          <option value="">All regions</option>
          <option>North Goa</option>
          <option>South Goa</option>
          <option>Central Goa</option>
        </select>
        <label class="sr-only" for="audience-filter">Filter by trip type</label>
        <select id="audience-filter" data-audience>
          <option value="">All trip styles</option>
          <option value="family">Family</option>
          <option value="couples">Couples</option>
          <option value="boutique">Boutique</option>
          <option value="beach-resorts">Beach resort</option>
        </select>
        <label class="sr-only" for="sort-stays">Sort stays</label>
        <select id="sort-stays" data-sort>
          <option value="order">Editorial order</option>
          <option value="name">Hotel name</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="tool-status">
        <span data-result-count>10 stays shown</span>
        <span>
          <span data-compare-count>0 selected</span> ·
          <a data-compare-link href="/compare/">Compare selected</a> (up to 4)
          <button type="button" class="text-button" data-clear-compare hidden>Clear</button>
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="tool-feedback" data-compare-feedback aria-live="polite" role="status"></p>
      <div class="hotel-list" data-hotel-list>
        {hotels.map((hotel, index) => <HotelRow hotel={hotel} position={index + 1} />)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <strong>More in this guide:</strong>
      <a href="#compare">Compare stays</a>
      <a href="#regions">Choose a region</a>
      <a href="#trip-finder">Find a base</a>
      <a href="#method">How we selected</a>
    </nav>

    <section id="compare" class="content">
      <h2>Compare before you choose</h2>
      <p>Select up to four stays above for a focused side-by-side view. Or <a href="/compare/">compare all ten hotels</a> in a compact table.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="regions" class="content">
      <p class="section-label">Start with the map</p>
      <h2>Which part of Goa fits your trip?</h2>
      <p>These are trip-planning distinctions, not guarantees about every locality. “Central Goa” is an editorial grouping for city and inland stays, not an administrative region. Distances and transport can shape the day, so check a property’s exact setting before booking.</p>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <article class="guide-card">
          <strong>North Goa</strong>
          <p>Consider it for a mix of popular beaches, restaurants and nightlife. The visitor circuit is varied, but places are spread across several settlements.</p>
          <a href="/north-goa-hotels/">Explore North Goa stays</a>
          <a href="/guides/north-goa-vs-south-goa/">North vs South guide</a>
        </article>
        <article class="guide-card">
          <strong>South Goa</strong>
          <p>A useful starting point for resort-led trips and time around the coast. Beaches and hotels can be far apart, so plan transport between areas.</p>
          <a href="/south-goa-hotels/">Explore South Goa stays</a>
          <a href="/guides/north-goa-vs-south-goa/">North vs South guide</a>
        </article>
        <article class="guide-card">
          <strong>Central Goa</strong>
          <p>May suit a city, heritage or inland itinerary more than a beach-first stay. This shortlist has two distinct central bases, so compare their exact settings.</p>
          <a href="/central-goa-stays/">Explore central stays</a>
          <a href="/guides/best-areas-to-stay-in-goa/">Read the area guide</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="trip-finder" class="content trip-finder">
      <p class="section-label">A starting point, not a ranking</p>
      <h2>Which part of Goa should you stay in?</h2>
      <p>Choose the main thing you want from the trip. The suggestions below use the locations and facilities in our researched shortlist; check each profile for its source and practical limitations.</p>
      <form data-area-finder>
        <fieldset class="finder-options">
          <legend>What matters most on this trip?</legend>
          <label><input type="radio" name="trip-fit" value="beach" /> Beach access</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="trip-fit" value="nightlife" /> North Goa restaurants and nightlife</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="trip-fit" value="small" /> A smaller-scale stay</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="trip-fit" value="family" /> Family facilities</label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="trip-fit" value="culture" /> A city or culture-led base</label>
        </fieldset>
        <button class="finder-reset" type="reset">Clear choice</button>
      </form>
      <p class="finder-prompt" data-finder-prompt role="status" aria-live="polite">Select one priority to see relevant areas and properties.</p>
      <div class="finder-results" data-finder-results aria-live="polite">
        <article data-finder-result="beach" hidden>
          <h3>Compare the exact kind of beach access</h3>
          <p>North and South both have distinct coastal bases. <a href="/hotels/taj-fort-aguada-goa/">Taj Fort Aguada</a> and <a href="/hotels/itc-grand-goa/">ITC Grand Goa</a> list direct beach access; <a href="/hotels/alila-diwa-goa/">Alila Diwa Goa</a> lists a shuttle to Gonsua Beach. Read the <a href="/guides/north-goa-vs-south-goa/">North vs South guide</a> before choosing.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-finder-result="nightlife" hidden>
          <h3>Start with the North Goa bases</h3>
          <p>The North Goa shortlist covers Vagator, Calangute, Nerul and Sinquerim-Candolim. <a href="/hotels/w-goa-vagator/">W Goa</a> is in Vagator and lists several dining venues; check current events, hours and transport for your dates. <a href="/north-goa-hotels/">Browse the North Goa stays</a>.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-finder-result="small" hidden>
          <h3>Look at scale as well as setting</h3>
          <p><a href="/hotels/ahilya-by-the-sea/">Ahilya by the Sea</a> describes nine rooms across three villas in Nerul. <a href="/hotels/amrapali-house-of-grace/">Amrapali • House of Grace</a> is an independent stay in Goa Velha, away from the beachfront resort strip.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-finder-result="family" hidden>
          <h3>Compare the facilities you will actually use</h3>
          <p><a href="/hotels/itc-grand-goa/">ITC Grand Goa</a> lists a children’s play zone, <a href="/hotels/alila-diwa-goa/">Alila Diwa Goa</a> lists a kids’ club and teen zone, and <a href="/hotels/taj-fort-aguada-goa/">Taj Fort Aguada</a> lists a kids’ activity centre. Confirm current operation and age suitability with the hotel.</p>
        </article>
        <article data-finder-result="culture" hidden>
          <h3>Consider a central base</h3>
          <p><a href="/hotels/panaji-residency/">Panaji Residency</a> is a city stay behind the Old Secretariat; <a href="/hotels/amrapali-house-of-grace/">Amrapali • House of Grace</a> is a riverside property in Goa Velha and is not beachfront. Explore <a href="/central-goa-stays/">central Goa stays</a> for this different itinerary.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <noscript><p>The finder needs JavaScript. You can still use the <a href="/guides/best-areas-to-stay-in-goa/">area guide</a> and compare the linked hotel profiles.</p></noscript>
    </section>

    <section class="content planning-guides">
      <p class="section-label">Useful before you book</p>
      <h2>Compare the stay, then check the details</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <article class="guide-card">
          <strong>What different hotel styles offer</strong>
          <p>Compare resort-scale properties, small independent stays and city residencies by setting and facilities.</p>
          <a href="/guides/goa-hotel-types/">Compare Goa hotel types</a>
        </article>
        <article class="guide-card">
          <strong>Seven checks before booking</strong>
          <p>Use a practical checklist for location, beach access, room terms, transport and current amenities.</p>
          <a href="/guides/before-booking-goa-hotel/">Read the booking checklist</a>
        </article>
        <article class="guide-card">
          <strong>Save a visual trip-planning guide</strong>
          <p>Download an original, photo-free pin graphic for the North/South decision and share it with a travel companion.</p>
          <a href="/pins/north-or-south-goa.png" download>Download the North vs South pin</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="method" class="content">
      <p class="section-label">Editorial approach</p>
      <h2>Why these ten made the list</h2>
      <p>We reviewed a broader pool of 21 candidate leads and retained ten where current official property details and a clear traveller use case could be confirmed. Because comparable independent review evidence, like-for-like rates and verified inspection data were not available for every hotel, we do not assign numerical scores or claim an objective ranking. The displayed order is an editorial reading order, not a quality score.</p>
      <p><a href="/methodology/">See the selection method, candidate notes and limitations.</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="content faq">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>Is North Goa or South Goa better for hotels?</summary>
        <p>Choose North Goa for a busier base near popular beaches, dining and nightlife. Choose South Goa for a resort-oriented stay and a slower beach holiday. The right choice depends on what you want to do most days.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are these the ten cheapest hotels?</summary>
        <p>No. This is a research-based shortlist across different property styles, not a budget ranking. We avoid displaying prices because rates vary by date, room and conditions.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I book rooms here?</summary>
        <p>No. This directory has no inventory or booking engine. Each profile links to the official property site so you can verify current rates, availability and terms directly.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script>
    const finder = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('[data-area-finder]');
    const finderPrompt = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-finder-prompt]');
    const finderResults = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-finder-result]')];
    const showFinderResult = () => {
      const selected = finder?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="trip-fit"]:checked')?.value;
      let found = false;
      for (const result of finderResults) {
        const visible = result.dataset.finderResult === selected;
        result.hidden = !visible;
        found ||= visible;
      }
      if (finderPrompt) {
        finderPrompt.hidden = found;
        finderPrompt.textContent = selected ? '' : 'Select one priority to see relevant areas and properties.';
      }
    };
    finder?.addEventListener('change', showFinderResult);
    finder?.addEventListener('reset', () => requestAnimationFrame(showFinderResult));
  </script>
</Base>
